    "problem_statement": "**Namespace declarations in XML parsing are reversed**\n\nI found a bug in the XML namespace handling. When parsing XML with namespaces, the prefixes and URIs are being swapped, causing incorrect parsing results.\n\nFor example, when I have XML like this:\n\n```xml\n<root xmlns:ns=\"http://example.org/ns\">\n  <ns:element>value</ns:element>\n</root>\n```\n\nThe namespace declarations are being stored incorrectly, with the URI as the key and the prefix as the value, instead of the other way around.\n\n**To Reproduce**\n\nHere's a simple example that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nimport xmltodict\n\nxml = '''\n<root xmlns:ns=\"http://example.org/ns\">\n  <ns:element>value</ns:element>\n</root>\n'''\n\n# This fails to correctly handle the namespace\nresult = xmltodict.parse(xml, process_namespaces=True)\nprint(result)\n\n# Expected output should have properly handled the namespace\n# But instead the namespace mapping is reversed\n```\n\nWhen running this code, the namespace handling is incorrect because the prefix-to-URI mapping is reversed internally.\n\nThis affects all XML parsing where namespaces are involved, particularly when using the `process_namespaces=True` option."
  }
